{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_slice_3", "label": "Slice 3 \u2014 The LOD Ladder, OBJ, and One Kernel Output", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Closes three places the codebase lied about itself: KernelOutput and MeshOutput were two unreconciled types, DerivativeStore had never run, and GET /api/blob/{blake3} did not exist."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_vertex_clustering_ladder", "label": "Vertex-Clustering LOD Ladder (L0/L1/L2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The whole ladder falls out of measure.rs's existing vertex-quantisation function at three grid sizes. Clustering does not need indexed input \u2014 it produces it \u2014 so Mesh stays an unindexed triangle soup and no re-parse or adjacency structure is needed. Grids are a fraction of the bounding box, not absolute, so a 5 mm screw and a 2 m gantry get comparable triangle counts."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_glb_writer", "label": "Hand-Written glTF 2.0 Binary Writer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "meshopt's Rust binding wraps C, which would put a C toolchain in the worker image and break the offline container build. Derivatives are designed to be thrown away, so writing plain GLB now and re-encoding in Phase 3 costs one regeneration pass over explicitly disposable data."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_process_takes_bytes", "label": "Kernel::process Takes Bytes, Not a Path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Ingest has already read and hashed the file, and reading it twice would be a second chance to read something different. Hashing before parsing is the ordering the whole pipeline rests on, so a kernel that re-opens the path can disagree with the hash already committed. The trait signature was the defect, not the code."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_output", "label": "KernelOutput (reconciled)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "entities stays Vec<Entity> rather than Vec<String> so Phase 3's measurement can snap to axes and radii instead of parsing 'CYLINDRICAL_SURFACE:22.000'. Its emptiness for mesh input is load-bearing: it is what stops tessellated numbers being presented as exact."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_blob_route", "label": "GET /api/blob/{blake3}", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "On the open path: it reads a derivative, never a source file, and never the kernel. Immutable caching is possible only because the URL contains the hash of what it returns."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_reachability_check", "label": "Blob Reachability Check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Content addressing is not authorization \u2014 hashes leak into manifests, logs, bundles and support tickets, so knowing one must never be a capability. An unreferenced hash is a 404 whether or not the bytes are on disk. Written now while it is one join, rather than retrofitted in Phase 8 as a security fix."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_migration_0004", "label": "Migration 0004 \u2014 Derivative Storage Discriminator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A derivative is stored inline or by hash, never both and never neither; and derivative.blake3 becomes a foreign key to blob, which is what makes ref_count cover derivatives and makes three identical rungs cost one blob instead of three."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_version_names_parser", "label": "kernel_version Names the Parser", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "derivative.kernel_version must change when output bytes could change, or a regenerated thumbnail is indistinguishable from a stale one. Once OBJ is ingested, a version reading stl-1 for an OBJ-derived thumbnail is exactly that lie, so the version names parser, tessellation writer and rasterizer independently."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_parse_obj", "label": "parse_obj", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_budget_retry", "label": "Triangle-Budget Retry (halve the grid)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Follows raster.rs's existing thumbnail retry pattern. DATA.md's ~5k and ~50k are approximate and the retry keeps them approximately true across a corpus where a fixed grid would not; the grid actually used is recorded in params_json so the derivative says how it was made."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_extension_dispatch", "label": "Format Dispatch on Extension, Not Byte Sniffing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "OBJ is plain text with no magic number, so a sniffing implementation reduces to guessing from the first non-comment line. The extension is what the walk filtered on, so it is what the parser is told; a file whose extension lies becomes a per-file Permanent failure."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_three_rungs_always", "label": "A Small Mesh Still Gets Three Rungs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The alternative puts a conditional into every consumer to save a few kilobytes on the smallest parts. Content addressing makes the waste nearly free: three identical .glb files are one blob with ref_count 3 \u2014 the rows differ, the bytes do not."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_slice_3", "target": "specs_2026_09_03_phase_1_slice_2_jobs_design_slice_2", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_vertex_clustering_ladder", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_mesh_kernel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_vertex_clustering_ladder", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_budget_retry", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_vertex_clustering_ladder", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_glb_writer", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_mesh_kernel", "target": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_kernel_trait", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_process_takes_bytes", "target": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_kernel_trait", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_process_takes_bytes", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_hash_first_short_circuit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_output", "target": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_kernel_trait", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_kernel_output", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_vertex_clustering_ladder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_blob_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_reachability_check", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_blob_route", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_derivative_store", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_lapidary_api", "target": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_blob_route", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-phase-1-slice-3-lod-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_04_phase_1_slice_3_lod_design_migration_00